  "product": "GTS",
  "name": "Vowel Pluck Bark",
  "author": "Riddim Rack",
  "description": "A short vowel bark on every note: each hit opens bright on an open, nasal vowel and snaps shut to a rounder 'oh' within a fraction of a second, like a mouth saying 'wow' in one syllable. A Mod Env sweeps the Formant filter, the low-pass on the second filter and the Reed layer's table position together, then settles, so held notes stay steady and mono over a clean sine sub at the played pitch. Play: staccato eighth-note and sixteenth-note riffs on F1 to A#1 at 140 to 150 BPM, one bark per note. Macros: Bark adds a second, deeper filter envelope for a harder snap, Vowel slides the resting vowel from 'oh' toward 'ee' while the tone opens up, Decay stretches the bark from a tight snap to a long, slow 'wow', Grit pushes the tube drive for a louder, rougher mouth.",
